.TH SYLVE-MCP 1 "@VERSION@" "Sylve MCP"
.SH NAME
sylve-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for Sylve FreeBSD clusters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sylve-mcp
[--config FILE] [--context NAME] [-n NODE] [-k] [--timeout SECONDS]
[--read-only] [--expose-tags TAG1,TAG2] [--expose-all] [-V] [-h]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sylve-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio that exposes the Sylve
Bhyve/Jail/ZFS cluster API to agents and models. It reads the same
configuration and bearer tokens as
.B sylve-cli
(see
.BR sylve-config (5)):
\f[BI]~/.config/sylve/config.yaml\fR plus the
.B SYLVE_*
environment variables.
.PP
The server registers curated cluster-aware tools (VMs, jails, ZFS, network,
backups, replication, tasks) plus three universal Swagger tools
.RB ( sylve_api_search ,
.BR sylve_api_schema ,
.BR sylve_api_call )
that together cover every operation in the bundled
.B docs/swagger.json
(336 paths, 441 operations).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
Path to the configuration file (default:
.BR ~/.config/sylve/config.yaml ).
.TP
.B \-\-context NAME
Named login context to use by default.
.TP
.BI \-n, \-\-node NODE
Default target cluster node hostname or UUID.
.TP
.BI \-k, \-\-insecure
Disable TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout SECONDS
HTTP request timeout (default: 30.0).
.TP
.B \-\-read-only
Refuse all non-GET API requests.
.TP
.BI \-\-expose-tags TAGS
Dynamically register one MCP tool per Swagger operation in these comma-separated tags (e.g. "VM,Jail").
.TP
.B \-\-expose-all
Dynamically register one MCP tool for every Swagger operation.
.TP
.BI \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-h, \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYLVE_CONFIG
Override configuration file path.
.TP
.B SYLVE_CONTEXT
Override active context name.
.TP
.B SYLVE_SERVER
Override server URL without a saved context.
.TP
.B SYLVE_TOKEN
Override bearer token without a saved context.
.TP
.B SYLVE_NODE
Default target cluster node.
.TP
.B SYLVE_INSECURE
Set to 1, true, or yes to skip TLS verification.
.TP
.B SYLVE_READ_ONLY
Set to 1, true, or yes to enforce read-only mode.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sylve/config.yaml
Configuration file containing saved login contexts and bearer tokens
(mode 0600). Create it with \fBsylve login\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.sp
.RS
.nf
sylve login https://sylve.example.test
sylve-mcp
sylve-mcp --read-only --context prod
sylve-mcp --expose-tags VM,Jail
.fi
.RE
.sp
MCP client configuration (OpenCode, Claude Desktop, Cursor) usually invokes
.B sylve-mcp
with:
.sp
.RS
.nf
{ "command": "sylve-mcp", "args": [] }
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sylve (1),
.BR sylve-config (5)